tion depending on implementation) because normalizeMetaSchemaUri does not accept null.', 'description': 'Ensure that passing a null IRI results in a predictable exception rather than silent failure.'}]}, {'group': 'Config propagation – null config', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'iri', 'value': '"urn:jsonschema:draft-07"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'A JsonMetaSchema is returned; loadMetaSchema receives null as its config argument. No NullPointerException occurs inside loadMetaSchema.', 'description': 'Validate that a null SchemaValidatorsConfig is forwarded correctly to loadMetaSchema when a new meta‑schema is created.'}]}, {'group': 'Cache miss – custom SchemaValidatorsConfig is propagated', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'iri', 'value': '"http://example.com/schema/custom-meta-schema.json"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig().setTypeLoose(false)'}], 'expected': 'A new JsonMetaSchema instance is returned. The loadMetaSchema method is invoked exactly once with the normalized IRI key and the supplied custom SchemaValidatorsConfig instance. The returned JsonMetaSchema holds the configuration passed (e.g., typeLoose = false).', 'description': 'When the IRI is not cached and a non‑default SchemaValidatorsConfig is supplied, getMetaSchema must forward that exact config to loadMetaSchema and store the resulting meta‑schema.'}]}, {'group': 'Cache hit – different config ignored after first load', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'iri', 'value': '"http://example.com/schema/custom-meta-schema.json"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'The JsonMetaSchema instance created in the previous test is returned. loadMetaSchema is NOT invoked again, even though a different (null) config is supplied. The configuration of the cached instance remains the one from the first call.', 'description': 'Ensures that after a meta‑schema has been cached, subsequent calls with the same normalized IRI ignore t