ema does not accept syntactically invalid IRIs and propagates an appropriate exception.'}]}, {'group': 'Trailing slash – treated as same meta‑schema', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'iri', 'value': '"http://example.com/schema/meta-schema.json/"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'The cached JsonMetaSchema for "http://example.com/schema/meta-schema.json" is returned. The trailing slash is stripped by normalizeMetaSchemaUri, so no new loadMetaSchema call occurs.', 'description': 'Confirms that a superfluous trailing slash does not create a distinct cache entry.'}]}, {'group': 'Concurrent access – loadMetaSchema invoked only once', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'iri', 'value': '"http://example.com/schema/concurrent-meta-schema.json"'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'When getMetaSchema is called from multiple threads simultaneously with the same IRI, the internal ConcurrentMap.computeIfAbsent guarantees that loadMetaSchema is executed exactly once. All threads receive the same JsonMetaSchema instance.', 'description': 'Simulates concurrent calls (e.g., using an ExecutorService) to verify the thread‑safety of the cache mechanism.'}]}]
